      "content": "Those who cling to trickle-down economics or deregulation often argue that markets naturally reward the strongest, yet they ignore how the relentless pursuit of shareholder ROI cradles the largest corporations for private gain while forcing ordinary citizens deeper debt and servitude. This logic implies that every individual must work twice as hard simply to maintain the status quo, effectively trading their freedom for a meager survival wage in exchange for the whims of the market. Such a framework is not freedom; it is modern serfdom that binds labor to machinery and the state to committee, leaving no room for human dignity or collective power. True economic sovereignty demands we reject these拐杖 chains and build a system where wealth serves life, not the other way around. Would you like to draft the next section focusing on concrete calls to action for these principles?",
